  "rationale": "Both candidates are direct matches to psoriatic arthritis at the EFO level, with endpoint-fidelity support from phenotyping_reported (PGS000342: “Psoriatic arthritis”; PGS001287: “Psoriatic arthropathy”). PGS001287 has substantially stronger PRS-comparable performance evidence than PGS000342, including explicit PGS-only AUROC=0.67648 and PGS-only R2=0.0335 (and full-model AUROC=0.72814 with only basic covariates: age, sex, array, PCs), whereas PGS000342 reports only a modest full-model AUROC=0.562 with unknown covariates and no PGS-only metrics. The heritability sanity check is consistent for PGS001287 (PGS-only R2=0.0335 is below the provided liability h2=0.0735). Limitation: PGS001287 comes from a pan-trait UK Biobank framework paper (“across 813 traits”), which domain guidance flags as often less reliable in external generalization than disease-focused scores; however, the competing disease-focused model here lacks comparable PRS-only metrics and shows weaker discrimination, leaving PGS001287 as the best-supported choice but with reduced certainty."
